2025/06/15 19:38:28.595655 client.go:276: LLM Request Body (TraceID: baa2bb6558f828297a0d908626f93df2): {"model":"gemini-2.5-pro-preview-06-05","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are Plandex, an AI programming and system administration assistant. You and the programmer collaborate to create a 'plan' for the task at hand."},{"role":"user","content":"hi"},{"role":"user","content":"test debug\n"},{"role":"user","content":"final test\n"},{"role":"user","content":"final test\n"},{"role":"user","content":"debug test final\n"},{"role":"user","content":"accumulator test\n"},{"role":"user","content":"stream debug test\n"},{"role":"user","content":"quick test\n"},{"role":"user","content":"FINAL FIX TEST\n"},{"role":"user","content":"FINAL FIX TEST\n"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Alright, let's run this final test. Based on the project documentation, it seems we're targeting a \"not-null constraint\" database error that was happening during plan branch creation. I'll also keep an eye on the data streaming and accumulator logic, as there are signs of recent debugging in that area as well.\n\nMy approach will be to:\n1.  Start the application in the local development environment.\n2.  Use the CLI to perform the sequence of actions that previously triggered the bug: create a project, create a plan, and then create a new branch from that plan.\n3.  Monitor the application logs for any errors.\n\nTo do this, I'll first need to load the relevant files to understand the application's structure, the specifics of the bug, and how to run the test.\n\n### Categories\n- Bug Analysis \u0026 Documentation\n- Application Execution \u0026 CLI\n- Server-side Plan \u0026 Branch Logic\n- Database Models \u0026 Migrations\n- Streaming \u0026 Data Handling\n\n### Files\n- **Bug Analysis \u0026 Documentation**:\n  - `commit_analysis.md` (Contains detailed analysis of the \"not-null constraint\" error)\n  - `atlas_issue_fix_local_mode.md` (Provides context on fixing the local development environment)\n  - `logfire_debugging_summary.md` (Details on logging and tracing which might be useful for debugging)\n- **Application Execution \u0026 CLI**:\n  - `app/start_local.sh` (Script to start the local environment for testing)\n  - `app/cli/cmd/new.go` (The `new` command, likely used to create a new plan)\n  - `app/cli/cmd/checkout.go` (The `checkout` command, used with a flag to create a new branch)\n  - `app/cli/lib/current.go` (Handles resolving the current project and plan, which is a prerequisite for testing)\n- **Server-side Plan \u0026 Branch Logic**:\n  - `app/server/db/branch_helpers.go`: CreateBranch (Core logic for creating a database entry for a branch, central to the bug)\n  - `app/server/db/plan_helpers.go`: CreatePlan (Logic for creating plans, which is a step before creating a branch)\n  - `app/server/db/project_helpers.go`: CreateProject (Logic for creating projects)\n  - `app/server/handlers/branches.go`: CreateBranchHandler (The API endpoint that triggers branch creation)\n  - `app/server/handlers/plans_crud.go`: CreatePlanHandler (API endpoint for creating plans)\n  - `app/server/handlers/projects.go`: CreateProjectHandler (API endpoint for creating projects)\n- **Database Models \u0026 Migrations**:\n  - `app/server/db/data_models.go`: Plan, Branch, Project, User, Org (The data structures for the database records)\n  - `app/server/db/db.go`: Connect, MigrationsUp (Handles database connection and running migrations)\n  - `app/server/migrations/2025032400_sign_in_codes_on_delete.up.sql` (Recent migration file)\n  - `app/server/migrations/2025031900_add_custom_model_cols.up.sql` (Recent migration file)\n- **Streaming \u0026 Data Handling**:\n  - `app/server/model/plan/tell_stream_processor.go`: processChunk (Relevant to potential streaming issues mentioned in prompts)\n  - `app/server/types/message.go`: StreamCompletionAccumulator (Relevant to the \"accumulator test\" prompt)\n  - `app/server/model/client.go`: CreateChatCompletionStream (Handles creating the stream from the model client)\n"},{"role":"user","content":"\nYou are an AI summarizer that summarizes the conversation so far. The conversation so far is a plan to complete one or more programming tasks for a user. This conversation may begin with an existing summary of the plan.\n\nIf the plan is just starting, there will be no existing summary, so you should just summarize the conversation between the user and yourself prior to this message. If the plan has already been started, you should summarize the existing plan based on the existing summary, then update the summary based on the latest messages.\n\nBased on the existing summary and the conversation so far, make a summary of the current state of the plan.\n\nDo not include any heading or title for the summary. Just start with the summary of the plan.\n\n- Begin with a summary of the user's messages, with particular focus on any tasks they have given you. Your summary of the tasks should reflect the latest version of each task--if they have changed over time, summarize the latest state of each task that was given and omit anything that is now obsolete. Condense this information as much as possible while still being clear and retaining the meaning of the original messages.\n\n- Next, summarize what has been discussed and accomplished in the conversation so far. This should include:\n  - Key decisions that have been made\n  - Major changes or updates to the plan\n  - Any significant challenges or considerations that have been identified\n  - Important requirements or constraints that have been established\n\n- Last, summarize what has been done in the latest messages and any next steps or action items that have been discussed.\n\n- Do not include code in the summary. Explain in words what has been done and what needs to be done.\n\n- Treat the summary as *append-only*. Keep as much information as possible from the existing summary and add the new information from the latest messages. The summary is meant to be a record of the entire plan as it evolves over time.\n\nOutput only the summary of the current state of the plan and nothing else.\n"}],"temperature":0.2,"top_p":0.2,"stream":true}
